      ],
      "mode": "All or Specific. Nothing else changes; a switch to All resolves the rule.",
      "all": "All shows the count badge and, while the list is absent or empty, Not resolved with a Resolve button.",
      "specific": "Specific shows the pick count and a pick of the domain's entities, filtered by the rule's device classes when it has any. Save writes entityIds in pick order, a repeat dropped.",
      "resolve": "An all rule's resolvedEntityIds: every entity id Home Assistant has with the prefix <domain>., sorted by code point; the device class filter is not applied. Written even when empty (the watch reads [] as none). When: the Resolve button, a switch to All, after an add (every all rule), and in the panel before a save for every all rule of a page the draft changed.",
      "resolveSample": {
        "states": [
          "light.example_study",
          "light.example_attic",
          "switch.example_heater",
          "binary_sensor.example_front_door",
          "binary_sensor.example_back_door",
